Dear @LaPinozPizzaInd , your mobile app is entirely inaccessible for blind & low-vision users relying on TalkBack, constantly prompting "No text found at that location." 

Digital accessibility is not an optional facility; it is a statutory legal mandate under the Rights of Persons with Disabilities (RPWD) Act, 2016 and the Information Technology (IT) Act. As per Government of India gazette notifications, compliance is mandatory for all service providers to ensure equal access for Persons with Disabilities (PwDs). 

Your current app UI violates these legal rights, completely excluding visually impaired consumers from your services. I strongly urge your legal and development teams to address this non-compliance immediately and ensure your application meets mandatory accessibility standards.
